  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Complex Root of a Cubic Equation</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;Determine in the form \(p + {@q*%i@}\) a complex root of the cubic equation \[ {@simpcubic@} = 0.\] &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt; - Recall that \(\sqrt{a} \) is  also rewritten as \( a^{@1/2@}\),  with \(a&gt;0\)  &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt; - Type your answer in one expression using STACK notation, For example: 2^(3/2) + i*2^(3/2)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt; - Do not separate expressions with commas or “or.”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br /&gt; [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:Result]]&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;b&gt;Worked Solution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consider the polynomial \( P(x)={@simpcubic@} \)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We observe that \( P( {@n1@})=0\). Then \({@n1@}\) is a root for \(P(x)=0\)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By dividing {@simpcubic@} by {@x-n1@}, we obtain \({@simpquadratic[1]@}\).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, \( {@simpcubic@} = ({@x-n1@})({@simpquadratic[1]@}) \) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since  \({@simpcubic@}=0\), then \( {@x-n1=0@} \) or \( {@simpquadratic[1]=0@} \)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let solve \( {@simpquadratic[1]=0@} \). When we compute its discriminant \(\Delta=b^2-4ac\) with \(b={@bcoeff@}, a={@acoeff@}, c={@ccoeff@}\) we get, \(\Delta ={@bcoeff^2-4*acoeff*ccoeff@}&lt;0\)&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;So the equation \( {@simpquadratic[1]=0@} \) admits two distinct complex roots satisfying the formula; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; \[x=\frac{-b±\sqrt{- \Delta} {@%i@}}{2a}\] &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; \[x=\frac{{@if bcoeff&lt;0 then "+" else "-"@}{@abs(bcoeff)@}±\sqrt{{@-(bcoeff^2-4*acoeff*ccoeff)@}} {@%i@}}{{@2*acoeff@}}\] &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;\[x = {@z1@} \; \text{or} \;{@z2@}\]&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </generalfeedback>
